  "slug": "me-aburre-me-molesta",
  "titulo": "Something bores, annoys or saddens you",
  "subtitulo": "Me aburre el golf. Me molesta el ruido.",
  "foto": "t01.jpg",
  "regla": "Aburrir, molestar, entristecer, preocupar and enojar work like gustar: the thing that causes the feeling is the subject, and the person is me / te / le / nos / les: me aburre el golf, nos molestan los mosquitos.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": null,
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "In English the person is the subject: _I'm bored by golf_. In Spanish the **thing** is the subject and the person is the **indirect pronoun**, as with **gustar**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "me / te / le / nos / les",
            "+ verb (3rd person) +",
            "thing or infinitive"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Verb",
            "Meaning",
            "Example"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "aburrir",
              "_to bore_",
              "Me aburre el golf."
            ],
            [
              "molestar",
              "_to bother, annoy_",
              "Me molesta el ruido."
            ],
            [
              "entristecer",
              "_to sadden_",
              "Me entristece esa noticia."
            ],
            [
              "preocupar",
              "_to worry_",
              "Nos preocupa la renta."
            ],
            [
              "enojar",
              "_to make angry_",
              "Le enoja esperar."
            ],
            [
              "chocar (informal, Mexico)",
              "_to really annoy_",
              "Me choca el tráfico."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "The verb agrees with the thing: **me molesta** el ruido, **me molestan** los mosquitos. With an infinitive, singular: **me aburre** esperar."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Careful: **yo aburro** means _I bore (people)_. For _I'm bored by it_: **me aburre**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: the thing does it to you, so the thing gets the verb."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
